review='''Independent mathematics review74 — actual zero-safe bounce, rate and energy layer

Decision: ACCEPTED_MATHEMATICS_ONLY, with no mathematical repair. I reviewed the entire211-line exact module RAW fcec688033797683b44f279a4d22971598926e6af3e9682ad76493d37580937c at checked parent e91f9b3acfeea172c33053b28d88b7fea6e61e9d. The module is an uncommitted frozen candidate at this parent, not a verified science commit. The accepted prospective header74 is reused only for its mathematical signature review; the BODY is audited here independently. I did not read primary paper source or decoder verdict, and give no source acceptance.

The complete private literal and public header retain exactly hα,hαβ,hV,hH,hη,hβη with their original types. The expanded frozen literal and previously sealed3537-byte header match exactly. The private definition merely specifies c,h,R,S,rate,H and all ten clauses; it supplies no proof premise. The proof-local definitions and change target unfold that same specification. No extra caller, arbitrary gradient certificate or process law is introduced.

The internal analytic bridge is valid. Finite-dimensional real E supplies CompleteSpace. QuadraticRegularization.strongConvexOn_and_lipschitzWith_gradient_add_quadratic is applied with U=V,m=α,L=β,r=0,u=0. Its W(x)=V(x)+0/2||x||² is exactly V and its Lipschitz constant β+0 is β. Its inputs are the original C² hV and both genuine Hessian inequalities hH; nonnegativity of α and β comes from their NNReal types. This produces LipschitzWith β (gradient V), hence gradient continuity, internally. It does not strengthen the public assumptions. The BODY uses hV,hH,hη; hα,hαβ,hβη remain explicit source-standing callers.

Write c=y−η∇V(xRef), n=h(xRef,x)=∇V(x)−∇V(xRef), a=<p,n>, and R(n,p)=p−(2a/||n||²)n. At n=0, total real division and scalar multiplication give R(0,p)=p. For every n, R is reflection in (span n) orthogonal complement: Mathlib reflection in span n is 2 projection−id, and orthogonal-complement reflection is its negative. The inner product is real symmetric, so its singleton formula has the exact required orientation. The resulting linear isometry is involutive and preserves norm, including n=0. Directly for n≠0, <R(n,p),n>=a−2a=−a; the n=0 branch is zero on both sides. This checks clauses4–5 without a nonzero-normal premise.

Clause1 is jointly Borel in (xRef,x,p). Joint n is continuous; inner product, norm squared, arithmetic, total real division, scalar multiplication and product pairing are measurable. Total inverse on the real group-with-zero is Borel despite its singularity at0. No continuity of S is asserted. Clauses2–3 follow because rate=√η max(0,<p,n>) is jointly continuous, then Borel, on the stated finite-dimensional product Borel spaces. This distinction is necessary: in E=ℝ, V(x)=x²/2, xRef=0,p=1,α=β=η=1, S has momentum1 at x=0 but−1 at every x≠0. These callers therefore do not imply continuous bounce.

For clause6, S(x,p)=(x,R(n,p)) keeps x fixed, hence keeps n fixed at the second bounce; R involution gives S²=id. Clause7 preserves H=(η⁻¹||x−c||²+||p||²)/2 exactly: x and c stay fixed and ||R(n,p)||=||p||. H is the weighted SUM of the two squared individual norms, not a product-space max norm.

For clause8, √η≥0 ensures rate≥0. Pairing flips a to−a, so rate(Sz)=√η max(0,−a). The elementary identity max(0,a)−max(0,−a)=a gives rate(z)−rate(Sz)=√η a with the stated sign and scale, including a=0. Clause9 uses n=0 to obtain S(x,p)=(x,p) and rate=0 even when p is nonzero.

For clause10 put e=H(y,xRef,z0). Since η>0, η⁻¹≥0 and each squared norm is nonnegative, e≥0. If H(z)=e, then η⁻¹||x−c||²+||p||²=2e. Thus ||p||²≤2e and ||x−c||²≤2ηe. Taking the nonnegative square-root bounds gives ||p||≤√(2e) and ||x−c||≤√(2ηe); no positive-energy premise is needed. Gradient Lipschitz continuity and triangle yield ||n||≤β||x−xRef||≤β(√(2ηe)+||c−xRef||). Cauchy-Schwarz gives max(0,<p,n>)≤||p||||n||. Multiplying only by the nonnegative factors √η,β and the square-root bounds proves
  rate(z) ≤ √η β √(2e) (√(2ηe)+||c−xRef||).
Every factor, the initial1/2 in H, and both η scales match the literal. The envelope is constant on the whole exact energy layer for fixed y,xRef,z0; it is not yet a rate bound along a constructed random path.

Degenerate cases are valid. At e=0 the layer forces p=0 and x=c, so rate=0 whether or not n=0; zero energy must not be conflated with zero normal. Rank-zero E is allowed and all vectors, gradients and norms vanish. The endpoint αη=1 is allowed because no inverse of1−αη appears. η remains strictly positive. No positive dimension, strict step cap, extra derivative bound, integrability, domination, decay or differentiability of the bounce is introduced.

Fresh direct source elaboration used the real pinned Lean4.33.0 executable and original Lake LEAN_PATH/LEAN_SRC_PATH roots. PID19204 compiled the exact canonical10565-byte source to this review's own ActualBounceRate.olean and terminated EXIT0; this was no Lake build-cache replay and wrote no canonical olean. A separate audit-only driver re-elaborated all exact source bytes followed only by #print axioms for the public theorem, PID52720 EXIT0. The result uses precisely propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. Local fake-closure scan found0 hits and exactly one public theorem/one private literal specification. Original linter warnings about unused private specification binders and style are retained in complete terminal RAW logs; there was no failed mathematical or compiler route in this review.

This result is mathematics-only. The theorem supplies actual Borel bounce, continuous rate and deterministic energy-layer algebra. It neither constructs a path/clock/Markov kernel nor proves nonexplosion, invariance, a terminal law, full PBPS/SPHMC mains, implementation errors/caps, expected-query cost or actual-input composition. It has no ActualHarmonicFlow73 formal parent; that future composition remains a separate edge. No new source review, decoder, VERIFIED, PURIFIED, Exposition Seal, main/live, full-paper or Goal-completion credit is supplied. No canonical, ledger or Git files were changed. All finite mathematical inputs have exact RAW and CRLF-to-LF-only snapshots; mutable publication/cell/global ledgers were excluded.
'''
